WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.687
The Maryland Insurance Administration is the state agency that regulates insurance,

00:00:04.687 --> 00:00:09.374
headed by the Insurance Commissioner, who is appointed by the Governor.

00:00:09.374 --> 00:00:14.488
The Commissioner enforces the Insurance Article and the regulations adopted under it.

00:00:14.488 --> 00:00:19.175
The Administration licenses producers and insurers, examines insurers for solvency, reviews

00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:23.862
and approves policy forms and rates, investigates consumer complaints, holds hearings,

00:00:23.862 --> 00:00:27.697
issues orders and penalties and publishes regulations and bulletins.

00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:31.958
Theo will deal with the Administration as a licensee, as

00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:36.219
the person complaints about him are sent to, and as

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:40.480
the regulator whose rulings decide what his insurers may sell.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.789
A producer may act only for insurers authorized to do business in Maryland.

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:49.098
Soliciting, placing or collecting premium for an unauthorized insurer is prohibited, and the

00:00:49.098 --> 00:00:53.407
producer who does it can be personally liable for unpaid claims as if

00:00:53.407 --> 00:00:57.053
he were the insurer, in addition to license discipline and penalties.

00:00:57.053 --> 00:01:00.036
Checking authorization takes a minute on the Administration’s website.

00:01:00.036 --> 00:01:04.345
The exception is surplus lines, which applies to property and casualty risks placed

00:01:04.345 --> 00:01:08.654
through licensed surplus lines brokers when no admitted insurer will write them; it

00:01:08.654 --> 00:01:12.300
does not open a door for health insurance from unauthorized companies.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:18.231
Producers must keep records of their insurance transactions, including applications, correspondence, premium receipts

00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:24.161
and the appointment documentation from Lesson 51, and must produce them when the

00:01:24.161 --> 00:01:29.179
Commissioner asks; electronic records must be retrievable within ten working days.

00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:32.829
Appointment records are kept for five years after

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:36.479
termination, and other rules set their own periods.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:41.497
Unlicensed employees may perform clerical and administrative work, collect information, schedule

00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:46.515
appointments and refer customers to a licensed producer, as long as

00:01:46.515 --> 00:01:51.077
they do not solicit, discuss coverage terms or receive commissions.

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:54.727
The line is conduct, not title, and the

00:01:54.727 --> 00:01:57.920
licensed producer is responsible for supervising it.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.482
Compensation for selling, soliciting or negotiating insurance may be paid only

00:02:02.482 --> 00:02:07.044
to a producer licensed for that line, and a producer may

00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:11.191
share a commission only with another producer who is licensed.

00:02:11.191 --> 00:02:15.753
Section 10-130 allows renewal or deferred commissions to be paid to

00:02:15.753 --> 00:02:20.315
someone who held the required license and appointment when the business

00:02:20.315 --> 00:02:24.462
was written, so a retired producer may keep receiving renewals.

00:02:24.462 --> 00:02:29.024
It also permits payments to people who do not sell, solicit

00:02:29.024 --> 00:02:33.586
or negotiate, such as a bonus to a receptionist, provided those

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:37.318
payments do not amount to unlawful rebating or inducements.

00:02:37.318 --> 00:02:41.880
Theo cannot split his commission with Priya for enrolling her staff.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.295
A producer may not collect premiums or charges different

00:02:45.295 --> 00:02:48.710
from those the insurer has filed, with narrow exceptions.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:53.263
One exception permits a placement service fee of no more than 15

00:02:53.263 --> 00:02:57.816
percent of the premium when the insurer pays no commission on the

00:02:57.816 --> 00:03:01.990
policy; on a 1,000 dollar premium that ceiling is 150 dollars.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:06.164
Another permits passing through the actual expense of a client’s credit

00:03:06.164 --> 00:03:09.959
card payment, with disclosure of accepted payment methods and costs.

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:12.994
A producer licensed as an adviser may charge

00:03:12.994 --> 00:03:15.650
a fee for advice under that license.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:19.065
Any other charge added to a commissioned policy is

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:22.480
illegal compensation, however small and however willing the client.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.915
Premiums Theo collects belong to the insurer, and return premiums belong to the client.

00:03:27.915 --> 00:03:30.632
He holds both in a fiduciary capacity.

00:03:30.632 --> 00:03:35.291
Maryland regulations require premium funds to be kept in a premium account

00:03:35.291 --> 00:03:39.561
separate from operating and personal accounts; mixing them is prohibited commingling.

00:03:39.561 --> 00:03:44.608
Premiums from several carriers may share one premium account unless a carrier objects.

00:03:44.608 --> 00:03:49.266
Withdrawals are limited to paying carriers, transferring commissions actually or on average

00:03:49.266 --> 00:03:53.925
earned, with a carrier letter for averages, and returning premiums; the balance

00:03:53.925 --> 00:03:58.195
may never fall below the premiums, return premiums and deposits owed.

00:03:58.195 --> 00:04:03.630
Using premium money for rent, even briefly, is misappropriation and a ground for revocation.
